# Palisade — Guns Replace Melee (design + as-built)

Date: 2026-08-27
Status: implemented, builds clean, verified headless

## Decision

Retire the player's sword. Every player spawns with a gun rolled at random from a
**starter pool**, and the arena prize is a gun rolled at random from an **arena
pool**. Training bots keep their swords entirely — `EnemyController` combat is not
rewritten.

## Why

The joust (`SwordCombat.cs`) resolved fights in one exchange: `BaseDmg 35` ×
`SpeedDmgScale` at `SpeedForMaxDmg 16` — exactly `PlayerController.BhopMaxSpeed` —
times the 1.5× head multiplier = **123 damage against 100 HP, a one-shot**. Whoever
landed the first pass won, so a fight yielded one bit of signal and the 40 s hunt
phase was decided instantly.

Guns make time-to-kill a *dial* (damage × fire rate × mag), testable solo by
shooting a dummy and counting shots, and move skill expression onto the movement
system (bhop / wall-run / slide), which is the strongest thing in the project.

## Weapon pools

Random rolls are **shared**: the host rolls both indices once and broadcasts
`{"t":"loadout","start":N,"arena":M}`, so matches vary but are never lopsided.

### Starter pool

| Gun | Mode | Damage | Fire | Mag | Reload |
| --- | ---- | ------ | ---- | --- | ------ |
| MAC-10 | hitscan | 18 | 0.15 s | 24 | 1.6 s |
| Sidearm (`pew`) | hitscan | 22 | 0.22 s | 12 | 1.4 s |
| Shotgun | 8 pellets | 8 each | 0.80 s | 5 | 2.4 s |

### Arena pool

| Gun | Mode | Damage | Fire | Mag | Reload |
| --- | ---- | ------ | ---- | --- | ------ |
| AWP | hitscan | 55 | 1.20 s | 5 | 2.6 s |
| AK-47 | hitscan | 32 | 0.20 s | 30 | 2.2 s |
| Rocket Launcher | projectile | 80 direct + 50 splash (r 4.5) | 0.95 s | 4 | 2.8 s |
| Quad Rocket | projectile | 45 direct + 30 splash (r 3.5) | 0.30 s | 4 | 3.2 s |

Head 1.5× / legs 0.5×, reusing `SwordCombat`'s existing `HeadMinY 1.5` /
`LegsMaxY 0.4` thresholds so hit-location behaviour stays consistent.

Rockets apply `SelfKnockback` to the shooter, so **rocket jumping falls out for
free** on top of the existing movement system.

### Measured TTK (`test/TestGunRange.tscn`, vs 100 HP, perfect aim, standing still)

```
MAC-10   6-7 shots  0.85-1.02 s        Sidearm  5 shots  0.95 s
Shotgun  2 shots @3m 0.83 s / 3 @10m 1.65 s / NO KILL @25m
AWP      2 shots  1.23 s               AK-47    4 shots  0.67 s
Rocket   2 shots  1.07-1.72 s          Quad     3-4 shots 0.68-1.22 s
```

An earlier pass had MAC-10 at 0.52 s and AK-47 at 0.42 s — below human reaction
time (~250 ms), which reproduced the sword's "one exchange decides it" flaw. Their
fire intervals were slowed (0.09 to 0.15, 0.13 to 0.20) to land in the current band.

## The hook: spread scales with speed

Hipfire spread grows with horizontal speed and while airborne. Go fast and you are
hard to hit but cannot shoot straight; stand still and you are accurate but a
target. ADS (RMB) tightens spread and caps ground speed to 4.5 m/s.

The AWP leans on this hardest (`SpreadPerSpeed 1.10`): near-pinpoint standing
still, useless while running. The crosshair's gap tracks live spread, so the
tradeoff teaches itself with no tutorial.

**ADS is scope-only.** The AWP is the only gun in the pack with a scope, so it is
the only one that can aim down sights. `SetAiming` gates on `GunDef.CanAds`, and
everything downstream (spread bonus, speed cap, viewmodel pull-in, third-person
camera pull-in) keys off `IsAiming`, so that single gate covers all of them.

## Ammo and reloading

**There is no reserve pool.** A reload always refills the magazine to full, so a
player can never be starved of ammo. Manual reload (R) works at any time from a
partial magazine, and running dry auto-reloads after a dry-click so nobody is
stuck holding an empty gun.

`TestGunRange` asserts both rules per gun, plus the ADS gate.

**Hit zones are FOOT-relative with origin − 0.8 as the foot** (players and
dummies both centre a 1.6 m capsule on their origin): head band 1.35–1.6, legs
below 0.5. The visual head pokes above the collider, so "head" means the top of
the capsule — aim at the face.

## Architecture

`GunCombat.cs` is data-driven: a `GunDef` table keyed by id, with three fire modes
(`Hitscan`, `Pellets`, `Projectile`). `Rocket.cs` is the projectile — a swept
raycast per frame rather than a RigidBody3D, so a fast rocket can never tunnel
through thin geometry.

`SwordCombat.cs` **stays on disk** and is simply no longer instantiated by
`PlayerController`. Bots still use it, and deleting it would force edits across
`PlayerAnimator`, `PlayerHUD`, and `OnlineDungeonArena` for no benefit.

Shotgun pellets accumulate per-target before applying, so a blast produces **one**
`TakeDamage` call and **one** damage number rather than eight of each.

### Networking — no new damage path

Damage was already client-authoritative: `OnlineDungeonArena` damages the
opponent's local puppet, and `PlayerHealth.DamageDealt` relays
`{"t":"hit","dmg":X}`. Hitscan and splash both route through that unchanged.

Only two **cosmetic** messages were added: `{"t":"shot"}` (muzzle flash + shoot
pose on the opponent) and `{"t":"reload"}` (so the opponent can see the window to
push you). The `parry` / `parried` messages were removed, and the defender-side
block validation in the `hit` handler was dropped — there is no block against a
bullet.

`sword_claim` / `sword_awarded` are reused as-is for the arena gun.

## Animation — free, already owned

`UAL1_Standard.glb` (already loaded by `PlayerAnimator`) contained a complete,
unused pistol set, now wired in: `Pistol_Idle`, `Pistol_Shoot`, `Pistol_Reload`,
and the `Pistol_Aim_Up`/`_Neutral`/`_Down` trio feeding an
`AnimationNodeBlendSpace1D` driven by camera pitch, so the character tracks its
target with the barrel.

**Gotcha worth remembering:** Godot's GLTF importer strips a trailing `_Loop` from
animation names. The clip is `Pistol_Idle_Loop` in the file but imports as
`Pistol_Idle` — the original mapping silently failed to find it.

`Hit_Head` and `Hit_Chest` were also adopted from the same pack (previously
unused), so a headshot can read differently from a body shot.

**Known gap:** the pack has no aiming-locomotion clips, so the gun pose is lost
while sprinting. The fix is an upper-body bone-filtered blend over `spine_01..03`,
`clavicle_*`, `upperarm_*`, `lowerarm_*`, `hand_*`. Deferred — polish, not a blocker.

## Models and procedural gun animation

Styloo Guns Asset Pack (free, itch.io), GLB. **Zero animation clips** — but every
gun is modelled in separate parts, which is better here: `AnimateGunParts` drives
them from `GunCombat`'s own timers, so they stay locked to whatever fire rate and
reload duration are tuned.

| Gun | Slide / bolt | Magazine | Trigger | Pump |
| --- | ------------ | -------- | ------- | ---- |
| mac10 | `mac10derriere_low` | `mac10magazine_low` | `mac10trigger_low` | — |
| pew | `pewhaut` | `pewmagazine` | `pewtrigger` | — |
| shotgun | — | — | `shotguntrigger` | `shotgunpomp` |
| awp | `snipertendon_low` | `snipermagazine_low` | `snipertrigger_low` | — |
| ak47 | `akderriere_low` | `akmagazine_low` | `aktrigger_low` | — |
| rocketlaucher | `rockethaut_low` | `rocketbullet_low` | `rockettrigger_low` | — |
| quadrocket | `quadrocketderierre_low` | `quadrocketdevant_low` | — | — |

Slide snaps back on the shot and rides forward over the first 35% of the fire
interval; the pump racks on a sine over the whole interval; the magazine drops in
the first third of the reload and slams home over the last third.

**Orientation:** every Styloo gun is modelled barrel-along-`+X` (verified by
dumping all seven AABBs), so both viewmodel and hand model apply `+90°` Y to map
`+X` onto `-Z`. `test/TestGunOrient.tscn` asserts this — it re-measures each model
after rotation and prints `OK` / `*** WRONG ***` per gun.

**AABB bug found and fixed:** the first measuring helper merged *mesh-local* AABBs
without applying each part's node transform. These guns are multi-part models, so
that mis-measured them badly (the rocket launcher read 0.85 m instead of 1.18 m),
throwing off viewmodel scaling. Consolidated into one correct
`GunCombat.MeasureAabb`, which walks the hierarchy accumulating transforms.

**Material gotcha:** the pack's readme warns a metallic/roughness workflow washes
the colours out. `FixStylooMaterials` forces metallic 0 / roughness 1 as
recommended.

## HUD

- **Reload ring** — `StaminaRing` repurposed. Completely hidden while idle;
  appears the moment a reload starts and sweeps 0 to 1 over the gun's real reload
  duration, so how long you are defenceless is shown, not guessed. Amber normally,
  hot red when the reload was forced by a dry magazine.
- **Ammo counter** — bottom-right, flashes red when empty.
- **Crosshair** — gap tracks live spread; doubles as the spread debug readout.

## Reticle customisation (Settings → RETICLE)

Persisted in `user://settings.cfg` under a `reticle` section: colour (six
readable-against-torchlight swatches), size, gap, thickness, and centre-dot
on/off, with a live preview panel. The spread-driven portion of the gap is **not**
configurable — that is the accuracy mechanic being displayed, not decoration. An
empty magazine overrides the chosen colour to red.

